{"timestamp":"2026-10-16T08:05:05.376Z","ordinal":40,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a143be-44e0-7cb0-a31d-81523d9eec1f","call_id":"call_1b1abe84c5ba4288b8eae78e7d7da056","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"✔ The default environment has been installed.\n{\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"source_commit\": \"9852d8360f9519d21d11099b45f5deb8ba80cb28\",\n  \"environment_commit\": \"3552d5003a2485b6405805236d5c54e7ed42f097\",\n  \"sha256\": {\n    \"pixi.toml\": \"131fc78549d9fe54a3e6c055e59ef753b1794df77507777b21c9529a611e7b89\",\n    \"pixi.lock\": \"f8fff1394fbeaa2ab1c4993fceb0dd6463fe0c08c81fcda397f3e752a72c4249\"\n  },\n  \"environment_repository\": \"https://github.com/leej3/stamped-ai-research-next.git\"\n}\n# Scientific assessment context\n\nAssess the original NARPS Hypothesis 1: a positive parametric effect of potential gain in vmPFC for the equal-indifference group.\nThe original [analysis instructions](https://www.narps.info/files/narps_instructions_for_analysis_teams.pdf) require whole-brain-corrected inference.\nThe scientific task is in `input/study-task.md`.\n\nWorkers receive 54 participant gain-effect maps from team AO86 and the corresponding cohort metadata.\nPreprocessing and participant modeling are fixed; evaluate group inference conditional on those inputs.\nJudge whether the analysis handles the intended participants, image geometry, quality, gain scaling, uncertainty and anatomical interpretation appropriately.\nThe maps represent independent participants; runs have already been combined within each person.\nEvaluate exclusions, uncertainty and multiple-comparison correction against the actual method.\nDefensible approaches can reach different conclusions; matching a prior team's answer is not the criterion.\nKeep scientific validity separate from the frozen STAMPED assessment.\nCheck how image coverage and missing observations enter the analysis; whether spatial alignment, vmPFC definition, group-model assumptions and whole-brain correction support the claimed inference; and whether quality checks, uncertainty and figures make those decisions inspectable.\nDo not require a particular mask, atlas, model or numerical result.\nParticipant variance maps are absent; judge methods against the supplied data.\nmanifest keys ['capture_finished_at', 'capture_status', 'captured_at', 'declared_artifacts', 'entries', 'errors', 'git_dependencies', 'git_metadata', 'head_commit', 'kind', 'omissions', 'policy', 'schema', 'workspace']\ntarget None\ncounts None\nworker? None\nentries 1135\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/judge-targets/narps-neutral-r1-08-j02/content/workspace/.codex/hooks.json\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/judge-targets/narps-neutral-r1-08-j02/content/workspace/.entire/.gitignore\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/judge-targets/narps-neutral-r1-08-j02/content/workspace/.entire/logs/entire.log\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/judge-targets/narps-neutral-r1-08-j02/content/workspace/.entire/settings.local.json\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/judge-targets/narps-neutral-r1-08-j02/content/workspace/.git/annex/gitqueue.lck\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/judge-targets/narps-neutral-r1-08-j02/content/workspace/.git/annex/index\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/judge-targets/narps-neutral-r1-08-j02/content/workspace/.git/annex/index.lck\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/judge-targets/narps-neutral-r1-08-j02/content/workspace/.git/annex/journal.lck\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/judge-targets/narps-neutral-r1-08-j02/content/workspace/.git/annex/keysdb.lck\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practi