ry?\nstamped-checklist:must/004\tmust\tT.1,T.3,T.5\tAre version control systems such as `Git` used for code, text, documentation, and configuration files?\nstamped-checklist:must/005\tmust\tT.1,T.3,T.5\tAre version control systems such as `git-annex`, DataLad, or `Git` LFS used for large binary data?\nstamped-checklist:must/006\tmust\tT.1,T.3,T.5\tAre the exact environment specifications used to generate a set of results included in the provenance records to link computational actions to particular environments?\nstamped-checklist:must/007\tmust\tA.1\tIs a `README.md` or `Makefile` included with instructions for installation and usage?\nstamped-checklist:must/008\tmust\tA.1\tIs there a clear starting point for users to start reproducing results (e.g., a main script, a workflow definition, or a container image)?\nstamped-checklist:must/009\tmust\tP.1\tAre relative paths used in scripts, avoiding hardcoded or system-specific paths like `C:\\Users\\...` or `/home/user/...`?\nstamped-checklist:must/010\tmust\tP.1\tAre all software dependencies included in the environment specification, rather than relying on pre-installed tools?\nstamped-checklist:must/011\tmust\tP.1\tHave all assumptions about the host system's configuration been documented (e.g., specific OS versions, required system libraries, or environment variables)?\nstamped-checklist:must/012\tmust\tP.2\tIs there a clear list of system requirements and dependencies documented in the README or environment specifications?\nstamped-checklist:must/013\tmust\tP.3\tAre environment specifications (e.g., Dockerfiles, `pyproject.toml`, `package.json`) included in the version control system alongside code and data?\nstamped-checklist:must/014\tmust\tP.3\tIs there a process for updating environment specifications when dependencies change, and are these updates tracked in version control?\nstamped-checklist:must/015\tmust\tD.1\tAre environment specifications (e.g., container digests, frozen package manifests) included to ensure others can attempt to exactly replicate the environment?\nstamped-checklist:must/016\tmust\tD.1\tAre environment specifications shared in a way that others can access and use them (e.g., published container images, archived environment files)?\nstamped-checklist:must/017\tmust\tD.1\tIs there documentation on how to obtain and use the environment specifications for reproduction?\nstamped-checklist:should/001\tshould\tT.2\tIs a common version control system (e.g., `Git`, DVC, `git-annex`, or DataLad) used across all components?\nstamped-checklist:should/002\tshould\tA.2\tIs the workflow tested regularly to ensure instructions remain accurate?\nstamped-checklist:should/003\tshould\tM.1\tAre raw data, processed data, code, and environment definitions separated into distinct modules?\nstamped-checklist:should/009\tshould\tM.4\tAre restricted data or software kept in their own modules?\nstamped-checklist:should/004\tshould\tE.1\tIs the pipeline tested in a fresh container, batch job, clean virtual machine, or cloud-based instance?\nstamped-checklist:should/005\tshould\tE.1\tDoes the workflow spawn disposable environments for each execution, allowing for isolation of runs?\nstamped-checklist:should/006\tshould\tD.2\tAre the exact environment specifications used to generate a specific set of results regularly tested to ensure they can be reconstituted as intended?\nstamped-checklist:should/007\tshould\tD.2\tAre environment artifacts archived within the research object where possible (e.g., executable binaries, container images)?\nstamped-checklist:should/008\tshould\tD.2\tIs there a process for updating environment specifications when dependencies change, and are these updates tracked in version control?\nstamped-checklist:may/001\tmay\tM.2\tAre external datasets or software dependencies included as submodules or linked as submodules?\nstamped-checklist:may/002\tmay\tM.2\tIs the modular structure documented to clarify how components relate and can be recombined?\nstamped-checklist:may/003\tmay\tM.2\tAre modular boundaries defined in a way that allows independent updates without breaking the overall workflow?\nstamped-checklist:may/004\tmay\tM.2\tIs there a clear mechanism for composing modules together (e.g., `git` submodules, or container orchestration)?\nstamped-checklist:may/005\tmay\tM.2\tIs there documentation or tooling to support users in understanding and navigating the modular structure?\n{\n  \"object\": {\n    \"path\": \"/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/judge-targets/narps-neutral-r1-08-j02/content/workspace\",\n    \"commit\": \"eece8595d255a766517e32ff10b2e6574d3c4e6a\",\n    \"is_datalad\": false\n  },\n  \"checklist_version\": \"0.3.1\",\n  \"probes\": [\n    {\n      \"probe\": \"ci-present\",\n      \"status\": \"not-checked\",\n      \"items\": [\n        \"stamped-checklist:should/002\",\n        \"stamped-checklist:should/006\"\n      ],\n      \"reason\": \"No recognized CI configuration; inspect equivalent repeated-testing records.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"uri\": \"probe:ci-present\",\n          \"description\": \"no tracked .github/workflows/, .gitlab-ci.yml, .circleci/, .forgejo/workflows/, .gitea/workflows/ in 58 tracked paths\",\n          \"sha256\": null\n        }\n      ],\n      \"details\": {\n        \"configs\": []\n      },\n      \"item_status\": {\n        \"stamped-checklist:should/002\": \"not-checked\",\n        \"stamped-checklist:should/006\": \"not-checked\"\n      },\n      \"item_reason\": {\n        \"stamped-checklist:should/002\": \"No recognized CI configuration; inspect equivalent repeated-testing records.\",\n        \"stamped-checklist:should/006\": \"No recognized CI configuration; inspect equivalent environment-reconstitution records.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"probe\": \"clone-weight\",\n      \"status\": \"met\",\n      \"items\": [],\n      \"reason\": \"No text blob in git exceeds 10 MiB.\",\n      \"evidenc