ata are included under input/; no external dataset route is needed. |\n| must/003 | S.1 | unmet | judgement | `analysis.py`, `delivery inventory` | analysis.py imports external Python packages, but no delivered environment spec or linked software module includes them. |\n| must/004 | T.1,T.3,T.5 | partial ⚠ (a MUST is not satisfied by partial) | probe:tree-clean | `probe:tree-clean`, `worker-end-state.json` | Git is used, but analysis.py, REPORT.md, figures/ and results/ were untracked at worker stop. |\n| must/005 | T.1,T.3,T.5 | met | probe:large-in-annex+judgement | `input/data/`, `worker-end-state.json` | The 54 participant maps are git-annex pointers with in-boundary payloads; map identities match the stop receipt. |\n| must/006 | T.1,T.3,T.5 | unmet | probe:run-env-linked+judgement | `analysis.py`, `results/summary.json`, `delivery inventory` | Shipped results have no worker run record linking the analysis action to an exact environment. |\n| must/007 | A.1 | unmet | probe:entry-point+judgement | `REPORT.md#Reproducibility files`, `delivery inventory` | REPORT.md names the script and says to use a supplied Python environment, but gives no install or executable usage instructions. |\n| must/008 | A.1 | met | probe:entry-point+judgement | `REPORT.md#Reproducibility files`, `analysis.py` | REPORT.md identifies analysis.py as the complete group workflow; the script is a usable starting point. |\n| must/009 | P.1 | met | probe:no-abs-paths | `analysis.py`, `probe:no-abs-paths` | The workflow builds input and output paths relative to its own location. |\n| must/010 | P.1 | unmet | probe:env-spec-tracked+judgement | `analysis.py`, `delivery inventory` | Required Python packages are imported by analysis.py, but no environment specification declares them. |\n| must/011 | P.1 | unmet | probe:platform-assumptions+judgement | `REPORT.md#Reproducibility files`, `delivery inventory` | The route assumes a supplied Python environment, but the delivery documents no OS, Python stack or host prerequisites. |\n| must/012 | P.2 | unmet | probe:platform-assumptions+judgement | `REPORT.md`, `analysis.py` | No clear system requirements or dependency list is delivered. |\n| must/013 | P.3 | unmet | probe:env-spec-tracked | `delivery inventory` | No environment specification is present in the complete worker delivery. |\n| must/014 | P.3 | unmet | judgement | `delivery inventory` | No environment update process is documented, and no environment specification is present. |\n| must/015 | D.1 | unmet | probe:run-env-linked+judgement | `delivery inventory`, `results/summary.json` | No frozen environment specification identifies the packages used for the shipped results. |\n| must/016 | D.1 | unmet | probe:env-spec-tracked+judgement | `.git/config`, `REPORT.md`, `delivery inventory` | No worker-declared route publishes an environment specification; the captured Git config has no remote. |\n| must/017 | D.1 | unmet | judgement | `REPORT.md#Reproducibility files`, `delivery inventory` | The report refers to a supplied Python environment, but does not say how to obtain or reconstruct it. |\n| should/001 | T.2 | met | judgement | `.git/config`, `input/data/` | One Git repository tracks code, inputs and configuration; git-annex stores the large map payloads. |\n| should/002 | A.2 | not-checked | probe:ci-present+judgement | `probe:ci-present` | No repeated-test history or schedule is recorded; such records would establish regular workflow testing. |\n| should/003 | M.1 | partial | probe:modules-separated | `input/, results/, figures/, analysis.py` | Inputs and generated outputs have separate directories, but code is at root and no environment module exists. |\n| should/004 | E.1 | not-checked | judgement | `replay record` | No fresh-environment run was attempted because the worker supplied no reconstructible environment; a clean run record would settle this. |\n| should/005 | E.1 | unmet | judgement | `analysis.py` | analysis.py runs in the active Python environment and does not create a disposable environment per execution. |\n| should/006 | D.2 | unmet | judgement | `delivery inventory` | No exact environment specification exists to reconstitute and test against the shipped results. |\n| should/007 | D.2 | unmet | judgement | `delivery inventory` | No environment image, binaries or archived environment artifacts are included. |\n| should/008 | D.2 | unmet | judgement | `delivery inventory` | No environment update process is documented; this duplicates must/014. |\n| should/009 | M.4 | not-applicable | judgement | `input/sources.json`, `input/participants.tsv` | N/A: the supplied anonymized NARPS derivatives and software have no identified restricted component. |\n| may/001 | M.2 | not-applicable | probe:subdatasets-resolvable+judgement | `.git/config`, `analysis.py` | N/A: there are no independently maintained project modules; package dependencies are not project modules. |\n| may/002 | M.2 | partial | judgement | `REPORT.md#Reproducibility files`, `workspace layout` | REPORT.md identifies the input, workflow, result maps and figures, but does not document their modular composition. |\n| may/003 | M.2 | partial | judgement | `analysis.py`, `workspace layout` | Inputs, code and outputs are separated by path, but the workflow has no environment boundary or documented component interface. |\n| may/004 | M.2 | not-applicable | judgement | `workspace inventory` | N/A: the object has no independently composed modules. |\n| may/005 | M.2 | met | judgement | `REPORT.md#Reproducibility files` | REPORT.md explains the main script and enumerates the result and figure files for navigation. |\ncapture {'url': None, 'commit': 'eece8595d255a766517e32ff10b2e6574d3c4e6a', 'captured_at': '2026-10-16T08:06:17+00:00', 'kind': 'study', 'capture': {'uri': '/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/judge-targets/narps-neutral-r1-08-j02/manifest.json', 'sha256': '2afd81ca5fdfaa03e85f2d3e65b04aac9f4b3d90eb39f95c24972